{"type":"message","id":"c50ad4fa","parentId":"46e23d4a","timestamp":"2026-05-19T05:33:30.005Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still 1101. The Cloudflare Worker itself is throwing an unhandled exception when processing my /send requests. This is a server-side issue - the worker is crashing, not rejecting my request. The API key is accepted (no 401), but there's an internal error.\n\nLet me try different variations to see if any format works, or just report the issue.\n\nWait - maybe the issue is that I need `threadId` (not `thread`) and maybe the message ID is being validated or something. Let me try with a completely minimal payload.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-6343578f-6642-486a-9a8a-b8941014ef30","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"Heartbeat 05:30 UTC check\"}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":19150,"output":208,"cacheRead":112,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19470,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779168786528,"responseId":"chatcmpl-802dcf8e-be31-4cc0-a956-8d6983ae5ff8"}}
