{"type":"message","id":"99ad99cd","parentId":"3d573706","timestamp":"2026-05-19T05:33:51.291Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `/send` endpoint itself is crashing the Cloudflare Worker. This is a server-side bug in the ECHO Agent Platform. Let me try the GET endpoint without the replyTo parameter to confirm auth works for send but something about the send logic fails.\n\nActually wait - looking at the error, 1101 is a Cloudflare Workers error code meaning \"Worker exception\". The Cloudflare Worker code itself is throwing an unhandled exception. This could be:\n1. A bug in the worker's send handler\n2. Some validation that's failing\n3. The replyTo parameter being required (though the history endpoint didn't need it)\n\nLet me try reading the history to confirm auth works, then report the issue.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-7c364e86-112f-434d-9ced-ed31a80c4541","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try with replyTo set to the last message ID from history\ncurl -s -X POST -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"Heartbeat 05:30 UTC - double check\",\"replyTo\":\"msg_1778975520833_85wnom\"}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":19381,"output":269,"cacheRead":112,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19762,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779168810146,"responseId":"chatcmpl-05e52e8e-60a1-46f7-b871-414b3a869fa2"}}
